In `format_as_emotion`, responsive list or breakpoint values are first converted into `mbps`, then for non-pseudo-selector keys the code loops over `mbps.items()` and executes `emotion_style.setdefault(mq, {}).update(style_sub_dict)`. Because `setdefault` is used, the line is designed to handle both cases: `mq` absent (insert a new empty dict) and `mq` already present (reuse the existing dict and update it). The test suite includes multiple inputs with more than one responsive property sharing the same breakpoints, so after the first responsive property creates entries like `"@media screen and (min-width: 0)"`, later responsive properties reach the same line with that same `mq` already present in `emotion_style`. Therefore `mq not in emotion_style` does not hold for every evaluation.

